        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45161.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5165658694\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45161\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45161/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45161\">#45161</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue correctly highlights that web components overstates the level and intent of protection provided by the shadow DOM. I've taken issue posters words for that. Also noted that this presented shadow DOM as JavaScript API, but it has evolved since this was written to also have a declarative API.</p>",
