        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82733600?u=a47d499e71c005e0cd356bdfd689e0dce80dcc45&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes the previously inaccurate \"border-box\" to \"overflow clip edge, which defaults to padding-box for non-replaced elements\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Makes the \"contain\" reference page more precise.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Does not mention the behavior of replaced elements, for which the overflow clip edge currently defaults to content-box, for two reasons:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It would make the description less concise.</li>\n<li>The behavior is still being worked out (<a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#overflow-clip-margin\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#overflow-clip-margin</a>).</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45101.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5128939431\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45101\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45101/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45101\">#45101</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45138",
            "title": "docs(css): Improve contain: paint's clipping bounds description",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T07:36:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T07:36:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "LukaJaredic",
                "url": "https://github.com/LukaJaredic"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44477.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4667059019\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44477\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44477/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44477\">#44477</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The History API pages claimed that <code class=\"notranslate\">pushState()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">replaceState()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">back()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">go()</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">forward()</code> throw a <code class=\"notranslate\">SecurityError</code> when called too frequently. Per <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4531528389\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12492\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/12492/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12492\">whatwg/html#12492</a> (merged 2026-06-16), the spec changed: the navigable's \"allowed to perform a navigation or history update\" algorithm now returns <code class=\"notranslate\">blocked</code> when the API is invoked too frequently, and the method silently returns instead of throwing.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I checked the current HTML spec before making this change: the shared history push/replace state steps and the delta traverse steps both consult the navigable's allowed-to-perform check and return on <code class=\"notranslate\">blocked</code>. The remaining <code class=\"notranslate\">SecurityError</code> cases (document not fully active, invalid/cross-origin URL) are unchanged.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes (5 pages):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">History/pushState</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">History/replaceState</code>: removed \"or if the method is called too frequently\" from the <code class=\"notranslate\">SecurityError</code> description; added a note that rate-limited calls are silently ignored, with the rate limit being implementation-defined.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">History/back</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">History/go</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">History/forward</code>: removed the sentence about throwing/warning/ignoring on throttling; added the same note.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The pages described behavior that no longer matches the spec or current Chromium behavior, which misled developers who relied on catching a <code class=\"notranslate\">SecurityError</code> to detect rate limiting.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45132",
            "title": "docs: history APIs silently no-op on rate limiting per spec",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T08:21:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T03:44:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "fufu1209",
                "url": "https://github.com/fufu1209"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96412244?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes the sidebar group macro on the <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code> page from <code class=\"notranslate\">{{APIRef(\"DOM\")}}</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">{{APIRef(\"HTML DOM\")}}</code>, so the sidebar shows \"HTML DOM API\" instead of the misleading \"Document Object Model (DOM)\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window\" rel=\"nofollow\">HTML Standard: the <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code> object</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-window\" rel=\"nofollow\">DOM Standard interfaces list</a> (does not include <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45123.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5146323062\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45123\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45123/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45123\">#45123</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45129",
            "title": "Fix incorrect sidebar group on Window pages",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-16T22:54:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T02:49:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "maitreyi03",
                "url": "https://github.com/maitreyi03"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96412244?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrects an invalid CSS media feature name in the <code class=\"notranslate\">@custom-media</code> example. The example used <code class=\"notranslate\">not (script)</code>, but <code class=\"notranslate\">script</code> is not a valid media feature, it should be <code class=\"notranslate\">not (scripting)</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/scripting\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">scripting</code> media feature reference</a> for the valid feature name and its accepted values.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45125.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5147382743\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45125\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45125/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45125\">#45125</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45127",
            "title": "Fix incorrect media feature name in @custom-media example",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T02:39:05.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T02:37:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "maitreyi03",
                "url": "https://github.com/maitreyi03"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43412.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4063297756\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43412/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412\">#43412</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family</code> page listed <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> as a plain generic-family keyword, but per the CSS Fonts 4 spec the script-specific generic font families use the functional <code class=\"notranslate\">generic()</code> syntax: <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(fangsong)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(kai)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(khmer-mul)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(nastaliq)</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Syntax section: <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: fangsong;</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: generic(fangsong);</code>.</li>\n<li>Values section: replaced the bare <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> bullet with the four script-specific <code class=\"notranslate\">generic()</code> families, described per the spec, with a note that they are not yet supported by any browser.</li>\n<li>Examples: removed the fangsong live-example block, since no browser supports the value.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page previously suggested <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> was a usable keyword value, which is not the case: the bare keyword is not in the current spec grammar, and no browser supports these values.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45124",
            "title": "docs: use generic() syntax for script-specific font families",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T08:21:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T01:44:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "fufu1209",
                "url": "https://github.com/fufu1209"
            }
        }
